===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To modify (a [[signal]], a [[graph]], etc.) to reduce a [[smooth]] [[curve]] to a series of [[discrete]] [[step]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|editors=Nikos Paragios; Yunmei Chen; Olivier D. Faugeras|title=Handbook of Mathematical Models in Computer Vision|publisher=Springer Science & Business Media|isbn=9780387288314|page=26|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=pPSK7_9R4IsC&pg=PA26&dq=%22staircasing%22&hl=&cd=12&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22staircasing%22&f=false|text=This leads to much smoother reconstructions in regions of moderate gradient and thus prevents '''staircasing'''.}}
# {{lb|en|real estate}} To [[increase]] one's share in a [[co-ownership]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Dave Cowan; Helen Carr; Alison Wallace|title=Ownership, Narrative, Things|publisher=Springer|isbn=9781137590695|page=139|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=aGRaDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA139&dq=%22staircasing%22&hl=&cd=11&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22staircasing%22&f=false|text=It is a good idea to make plans for '''staircasing''' when you first buy your shared ownership home.}}

