===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[File:31 FW conducts ACE training during Agile Wyvern 210907-F-ZR251-1155.jpg|thumb|a '''stake''' used to secure a tent to the ground]]

# {{senseid|en|pointed stick or similar object}} A [[piece]] of [[wood]] or other material, usually [[long]] and [[slender]], [[pointed]] at one end so as to be easily driven into the ground as a [[marker]] or a [[support]] or [[stay]].
#: {{ux|en|We have surveyor's '''stakes''' at all four corners of this field, to mark exactly its borders.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Metamorphoses|passage=A sharpened '''stake''' strong Dryas found.}}
# {{senseid|en|stick driven into ground in croquet}} {{lb|en|croquet}} A piece of wood driven in the ground, placed in the middle of the court, that is used as the finishing point after scoring 12 hoops in croquet.
# {{senseid|en|stick or sticklike object for body of vehicle}} A [[stick]] or similar object (e.g., steel channel or angle stock) [[insert]]ed [[upright]] in a [[lop]], [[eye]], or [[mortise]], at the side or end of a [[cart]], [[flat car]], [[flatbed]] trailer, or the like, to prevent goods from [[fall off|falling off]]; often connected in a grid forming a [[stakebody]].
# {{senseid|en|timber on which execution by burning happened}} {{qualifier|with definite article}} The piece of [[timber]] to which a person condemned to death was [[affix]]ed to be [[burn]]ed.
#: {{ux|en|Thomas Cranmer was burnt at the '''stake'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|publisher=Long|location=London|page=106|passage=However, the word "witch" came to be applied almost exclusively to women who [...] were usually old and ugly, and for this reason many unfortunate old ladies, whose only crimes were loneliness and a lack of beauty, went to the '''stake'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|a share or interest in a business or situation}} A [[share]] or interest in a business or a given situation.
#: {{cot|en|seat at the table}}
#: {{ux|en|The owners let the managers eventually earn a '''stake''' in the business.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 February 10|author=Richard Clinnick|title=Eurostar boost as French promise aid|journal=RAIL|issue=924|page=10|text=The French Government is Eurostar's majority shareholder, with the country's state-owned railway SNCF holding a 55% '''stake''', while Belgian state operator SNCB has a 5% '''stake'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|asset wagered}} That which is laid down as a [[wager]]; that which is staked or [[hazard]]ed; a [[pledge]].
# A small [[anvil]] usually [[furnish]]ed with a [[tang]] to enter a hole in a [[bench]] top, as used by [[tinsmith]]s, [[blacksmith]]s, etc., for light work, punching hole in or cutting a work piece, or for specific forming techniques etc.
# {{senseid|en|a Mormon district or its inhabitants}} {{lb|en|Mormonism}} A [[territorial]] [[division]] comprising all the Mormons (typically several thousand) in a geographical area.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1910|title=Schaff–Herzog Encyclopedia of Religious Knowledge
|passage=Every city, or '''stake''', including a chief town and surrounding towns, has its president, with two counselors; and this president has a high council of chosen men.}}

