#* {{RQ:Eliot Silas Marner|chapter=VIII|passage=You see, I'd made a bargain with him to buy the horse for a hundred and twenty—a swinging price, but I always liked the horse. And what does he do but go and '''stake''' him—fly at a hedge with stakes in it, atop of a bank with a ditch before it.}}
