|passage=“You ladies happen to notice what happened to this vampire? This just happened. Did you see who '''staked''' him?”}}
# {{senseid|en|put at risk by pledge or wager}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To put [[at risk]] upon [[success]] in [[competition]], or upon a future [[contingency]].
#: {{syn|en|bet|hazard|wager}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Pastorals|page=725|passage=I'll '''ſtake''' my Lamb that near the Fountain plays, / And from the Brink his dancing Shade ſurveys.}}
# {{senseid|en|provide capital to}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To provide (another) with money in order to engage in an activity as [[betting]] or a business venture.
#: {{ux|en|John went broke, so to keep him playing, Jill had to '''stake''' him.}}
#: {{ux|en|His family '''staked''' him $10,000 to get his business started.}}
# {{senseid|en|put cryptocurrency coins at risk}} {{lb|en|cryptocurrency}} To deposit and risk a considerable amount of [[cryptocurrency]] in order to participate in the [[proof of stake]] process of verification.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Elad Elrom|title=The Blockchain Developer{{...|: A Practical Guide for Designing, Implementing, Publishing, Testing, and Securing Distributed Blockchain-based Projects}}|publisher=Apress|isbn=9781484248478|page=23|chapter=Blockchain Basics|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=6c2kDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA23&dq=%22staking%22+coins&hl=&cd=11&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22staking%22%20coins&f=false|text=Any peer can participate in the mining process by '''staking''' coins in order to validate a new transaction. To become a miner, there are two options; you can '''stake''' your coins to be used by a trustworthy node {{...}}, or you can submit a full node to be selected as a miner.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|glovemaking}} To stretch leather skin over a piece of iron held knee-height, in preparation to use the skin in the creation of gloves.

