|passage=Localities across New Jersey imposed curfews to prevent looting. In Monmouth, Ocean and other counties, people waited for hours for gasoline at the few '''stations''' that had electricity. Supermarket shelves were stripped bare.}}
# A place where workers are stationed.
## An [[official]] [[building]] from which [[police]] or [[firefighter]]s operate.
##: {{ux|en|The police '''station''' is opposite the fire '''station'''.}}
## A place where one performs a task or where one is on call to perform a task.
