## A military base.
##: {{ux|en|She had a boyfriend at the '''station'''.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 November 29|author=Philip Haigh|title=New Piccadilly Line trains put to the test|journal=RAIL|issue=997|page=26|text=The dynamic tests at Wildenrath use continuous test tracks built on the site of a former Royal Air Force '''station''' that was vacated after the end of the Cold War.}}
## A place used for [[broadcast]]ing radio or television; the broadcasting entity itself.
##: {{ux|en|I used to work at a radio '''station'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|I used to listen to that radio '''station'''.}}
## {{lb|en|computing}} A [[device]] communicating over a [[network]]; a [[host]].
##: {{ux|en|An Econet network is made up of a number of '''stations'''.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Colin Woodcock|title=The ZX Spectrum on Your PC|page=16
|passage=When entering a LOAD/SAVE/FORMAT, etc command you not only had to identify the destination of the data (ie, microdrive, network or RS232), but the number of the drive or '''station''' too.}}
