# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[coastal]] [[landform]], consisting of a large [[vertical]] [[column]] of [[rock]] in the sea.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1828|author=w:Thomas Keightley|title=The Fairy Mythology|volume=I|location=London|publisher=William Harrison Ainsworth|page=266|passage=A boat's-crew landed one time upon one of the '''stacks''' with the intention of attacking the seals.}}
# {{senseid|en|library}} {{lb|en|library}} Compactly spaced [[bookshelf|bookshelves]] used to house large collections of [[books]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=The Magnetic Fields|title=Holiday|chapter=Swinging London|passage=You took me to your library and kissed me in the '''stacks'''.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A large amount of an object.
#: {{ux|en|They paid him a '''stack''' of money to keep quiet.}}
# {{lb|en|military}} A pile of [[rifle]]s or [[musket]]s in a cone shape.
